payload.message:
The repo confirms the waste is structural, not just prompt tuning: the bootstrap prompt currently mandates up to five calls even though a new session-start hook already loads the learner profile and goals automatically. Several NodePod and project tools are also advertised when their backing runtime is unavailable, so the model spends attention on capabilities that can only return “not active.”

The clean boundary I’m converging on is:

- hooks assemble context and record evidence;
- OpenUI owns interaction state and user actions;
- tools are reserved for external capabilities or consequential side effects;
- commands/panels own inspection and maintenance.

Two product choices materially affect the final migration map.

